    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `TokenizerManagerScoreMixin._anchor_counts_per_item` (`python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager_score_mixin.py`), counting how many anchor token positions strictly fall inside each item boundary `(lo, hi)` previously scanned the entire `anchor_positions` list per item:\n\n```python\nsum(1 for p in anchor_positions if lo < p < hi)\n```\n\nBecause `anchor_positions` is produced by `_find_subsequence_positions` scanning left-to-right (`range(0, n - m + 1)`), it is guaranteed to be strictly sorted in ascending order. Replacing the per-item $O(A)$ generator scan with `bisect_left(anchor_positions, hi) - bisect_right(anchor_positions, lo)` reduces multi-item anchor counting from $O(I \\cdot A)$ to $O(I \\log A)$ while preserving identical strict-interior `(lo < p < hi)` semantics.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Import `bisect_left` and `bisect_right` from `bisect` in `python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager_score_mixin.py`.\n- Replace the per-item linear generator scan in `_anchor_counts_per_item` with `bisect_left(anchor_positions, hi) - bisect_right(anchor_positions, lo)`.\n- Add `test_anchor_counts_per_item_many_items_and_boundary_anchors` in `test/registered/unit/managers/test_setwise_score_mixin.py` verifying strict-interior boundary exclusions (`lo` and `hi` excluded) across multi-item scoring inputs.\n\n## Accuracy & Verification\n\n- `pytest test/registered/unit/managers/test_setwise_score_mixin.py`: 51 passed.\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nBuilds on the setwise scoring and multi-item scoring (`--enable-mis`) infrastructure authored by @sundar24295s (#38965, #41188), @mickqian (#40826), @chuanrui (#39730), and @rwang5203 (#42183).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #40428009378](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40428009378)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #40428009309](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40428009309)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #40428009467](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40428009467)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
